# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ChessProphy — environment
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is gitignored except this file.
#
# EVERY variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set, the app runs
# local-first: progress persists to the browser's storage and no network call
# is made. See supabase/README.md for what changes when a backend is connected.
#
# Only variables prefixed VITE_ reach the browser — that is a Vite rule, and it
# is the reason the service-role key must never be named VITE_ANYTHING.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hosted project: Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# Local stack:    printed by `supabase start`.
#
# The anon key is PUBLIC by design. It identifies the project, it does not
# authorise anything — every table is protected by row level security, so this
# key alone grants exactly the access an anonymous visitor should have.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Local defaults, for reference:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<the anon key `supabase start` prints>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER put the service_role key in this file, in any VITE_ variable, or in
# any file that reaches the browser. It bypasses row level security entirely.
# It belongs in CI/deployment secrets and nowhere else.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Dev server (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PORT=5173
